        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iran: Saudi Arabia warns of 'military action' over repeated attacks Middle East Issued on: 19/03/2026 - 12:18 Modified: 19/03/2026 - 12:32 Saudi Arabia warned that it had 'reserved the right to take 'military actions' over #Iran's repeated attacks on the kingdom, as fresh trikes hit Riyadh during a summit of regional foreign ministers. The comment marks a turn in the #Gulf's reaction to Iran's strikes on its neighbours since the start of the #war. Ayman Mhanna: 'Lebanon has become the theatre for a war between Israel and Iran' 19/03/2026 Middle East Qatar orders departure of two Iranian diplomats over gas facility attack 18/03/2026 Middle East 'Acute risk' that Iraq could become once again victim of internal conflict as Iran war progresses 18/03/2026 Middle East Iran did not try to rebuild enrichment after June 2025 attack, US intel chief says 18/03/2026 Middle East Both sides in Iran war ratchet up attacks on energy facilities, as oil prices surge 18/03/2026 Middle East Elisa Catalano Ewers: Israeli leadership moves to destabilise regime’s leadership structure 18/03/2026 Middle East Soler i Lecha: Foreign policy of Pedro Sánchez 'widely supported by the Spanish population' 18/03/2026 Spain Crowds gather for funeral of top security official Ali Larijani 18/03/2026 Middle East Beirut building collapses amid fresh Israeli strikes in capital city's centre 18/03/2026 Middle East"
